3.4 Nexus IQ “Component Unknown” for Confluent Kafka Libraries

One-liner: Resolved Nexus IQ “Component Unknown” violations for Confluent Kafka libraries by embedding an SBOM in the application jar, with zero pipeline changes.

Context:

Nexus IQ couldn’t identify Confluent libraries because they aren’t hosted on Maven Central. The standard CycloneDX plugin clashed with our Gatling plugin, and the Jenkins scan step couldn’t be changed.
I wrote a native Gradle task that generates a CycloneDX SBOM and embeds it in the jar, so Nexus IQ identifies those components by their coordinates. Maven publishing was not affected.
4. Spring Boot 4 / JDK 21 Migration
4.1 Jackson 3 Property Naming Change (Bill Pay)

One-liner: Kept existing API contracts intact through the Spring Boot 4 / Jackson 3 upgrade by building a Jackson 2-compatible naming strategy.

Context:

Jackson 3 changed how fields like eBillStatus appear in JSON, which broke API contracts with consumers. None of the configuration-only (application.yml) options restored the correct behavior.
I built a JacksonConfiguration class with a naming strategy ported from Jackson 2. I also found and corrected edge cases where our earlier custom naming strategy produced wrong names (e.g., eURL, iPhone).
4.2 Wires Production Issue – Default Value Lost After Upgrade

One-liner: Resolved a Wires production issue caused by a Jackson 3 null-handling change with a single, targeted configuration fix.

Context:

After the upgrade, the country = "USA" default stopped being applied when clients sent null.
I ruled out the code generator by comparing old and new generated classes, confirmed it was a Jackson 3 behavior change, and fixed it with a scoped mixin (@JsonSetter(nulls = SKIP)) in the existing Jackson configuration.
