6. Production Support
6.1 FIS mTLS Certificate Expiry Incident – Root Cause Analysis

One-liner: Led the root cause analysis for the October 2 FIS mTLS outage and put preventive controls in place for future certificate rotations.

Context:

Four Bill Pay APIs got 403 errors from FIS for about 90 minutes, starting the exact minute the old client certificate expired.
I showed the root cause was on our side. Running pods still held the old certificate loaded at startup. The FIS overlap window, when both old and new certificates were accepted, had hidden this until the old one expired. I ruled out the proxy, FIS and the trust manager.
Preventive actions:
mandatory pod restart with certificate-serial verification after every rotation
logging the certificate identity at startup
expiry alerts
rotating 30+ days before expiry
